  "text_md": "## CAT 125\n\nPublic Rhetoric and Practical Communication: Developing Expertise through Digital Media\n\nProf. Joe Bigham, Ph.D. dbigham@ucsdedu\n\nOffice: CAT Program office TA suite\n\nOffice Hours: Monday 1-3pm\n\nLecture: Tuesday 5-6:5Opm, Center 115\n\n## TA info:\n\n|   876962 | BO1   | TuTh   | 8:50a         | YORK   | 3050B   | mmandule@ucsd.edu   | Mandalay, Morgan   |\n|----------|-------|--------|---------------|--------|---------|---------------------|--------------------|\n|   876963 | BO2   | TuTh   | 9:O0a - 9:50a | YORK   | 3050B   | mmandule@ucsd. edu  | Mandalay, Morgan   |\n|   876966 | BO5   | TuTh   | 1:OOp-        | YORK   | 3050B   | gsrmabek@ucsd.edu   | Srmabekian, Gina   |\n|   876967 | BO6   | TuTh   | 2:OOp- 2:50p  | CENTR  | 201     | gsrmabek@ucsd.edu   | Srmabekian, Gina   |\n|   876968 | BO7   | TuTh   | 3:OOp- 3:50p  | YORK   | 3050B   | aprokop@ucsd.edu    | Prokopyev, Anton   |\n|   876969 | BO8   | TuTh   | 4:OOp-        | YORK   | 3050B   | aprokop@ucsd.edu    | Prokopyev, Anton   |\n|   876970 | BO9   | TuTh   | 7:OOp- 7:50p  | YORK   | 3050B   | jlfierro@ucsd.edu   | Fierro, Jaclyn     |\n|   876971 | B1O   | TuTh   | 8:50p 8:OOp-  | YORK   | 3050B   | jlfierro@ucsd.edu   | Fierro, Jaclyn     |\n|   876972 | B11   | TuTh   | 7:OOp- 7:50p  | YORK   | 4050B   | tOnguyen@ucsd.edu   | Nguyen, Ly         |\n|   876973 | B12   | TuTh   | 8:5Op 8:OOp-  | YORK   | 4050B   | tOnguyen@ucsd.edu   | Nguyen, Ly         |\n\n## Course Description:\n\nThis course in public rhetoric and practical communication examines the use of digital media as a demonstration of expertise; and gives students opportunities to create their own expertiserelated materials. Challenging the notion of expertise as a body of knowledge, we will consider expertise as a type of performance. This performance may be inscribed into a recorded form, such as a text or a YouTube video. It may also be performed for a live audience, as in a presentation: We will examine expertise demonstrations, how media affect the performance of expertise, and how individuals have created media-specific identities. Students will reflect on their own expertise; and learn how to efficiently demonstrate their authority through digital media. Students who have completed the 124 Practicum course are highly encouraged to focus on their practicum experience. blog\n\n## Course Website:\n\nImportant information for the class can be found on the course website at http:Llted ucsdedu: Your user name and password is the same used to login to Tritonlink. Make sure that you can",
